give the 3×3 motif.\n- The 6×6 bottom half is the placement map.\n- The motif is stamped into each 3×3 tile of the 18×18 canvas whose map cell is non-zero.\n\nIn pair 3 this gives the motif `1 0 1 / 0 1 0 / 3 3 3`. The map is a vertical stem of 2s in column 2 over a 3-wide base, so the output has a column of motifs at columns 6–8 and three motifs side by side on the bottom map row. That matches the expected output.\n\nFor the test, the divider is the row of 5s at y=6. The motif is `0 1 0 / 3 0 3 / 0 2 0`, and it is stamped wherever the cross-shaped map of 2s is filled.","code":"def transform(grid):\n    g = np.array(grid)\n    bg = 0\n    H, W = g.shape\n    div = None\n    # divider: uniform non-bg row whose colour occurs nowhere else\n    for y in range(H):\n        row = g[y]\n        if len(set(row.tolist())) == 1 and row[0] != bg and np.sum(g == row[0]) == W:\n            div = y\n            break\n    if div is None:\n        for y in range(H):\n            if len(set(g[y].tolist())) == 1 and g[y, 0] != bg:\n                div = y\n                break\n    top = g[:div]\n    pat = g[div + 1:]\n    ph, pw = pat.shape\n    f = max(1, top.shape[0] // 3)\n    motif = top[::f, ::f]\n    mh, mw = motif.shape\n    out = np.zeros((ph * mh, pw * mw), dtype=int)\n    emit(out, \"Allocate a blank canvas: the placement map (below the divider) scaled by the 3x3 motif size (top half downsampled from 2x2 blocks).\")\n    for i in range(ph):\n        stamped = False\n        for j in range(pw):\n            if pat[i, j] != bg:\n                out[i * mh:(i + 1) * mh, j * mw:(j + 1) * mw] = motif\n                stamped = True\n        if stamped:\n            emit(out, f\"Stamp the motif into every tile of map row {i} whose map cell is filled.\")\n    emit(out, \"Final canvas: one motif copy for each filled cell of the placement map.\")\n    return out\n","candidate_tactics":{"panels":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"The size error in pair 3 is caused by how the divider row is found, not by the stamping rule."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"My code took the first uniform non-background row as the divider, so it stopped at y=4 instead of the real divider at y=6."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"**Fix:** pick the divider by a property only the real divider has."}],"repeat":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"- The motif is stamped into each 3×3 tile of the 18×18 canvas whose map cell is non-zero."},{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Stamp the motif into every tile of map row 1 whose map cell is filled."},{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Stamp the motif into every tile of map row 2 whose map cell is filled."}],"template":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"That is the motif's bottom row `3 3 3` drawn as 2×2 blocks."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"The map then became too tall and the motif came out wrong."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"A row of 3s inside the motif fails the test, because 3 also appears in the next row."}],"dynamics":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"If no row passes, the code falls back to the old first-uniform-row choice."}],"count":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"Its colour fills that one row and appears nowhere else in the grid, so the count of that colour equals the grid width."}],"crop":[{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Allocate a blank canvas: the placement map (below the divider) scaled by the 3x3 motif size (top half downsampled from 2x2 blocks)."}],"scale":[{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Allocate a blank canvas: the placement map (below the divider) scaled by the 3x3 motif size (top half downsampled from 2x2 blocks)."}]},"provenance":{"reference_assisted":false,"query_labels_used_for_rule_diagnosis":false},"artifact_sha256":"28da0a212c80ee8c4e602b65faff6bd1153ab2e30d61b3ccda0ed192dba5b283","task_sha256":"6dcef3879b2abb4c31f4632d95b06121dc24fd43b6bb7d1dc840f6ae0b9b9aba","validation":"Frozen corpu